# Controls what the Vercel CLI uploads when deploying from a working copy
# (`vercel --prod`). Git-triggered deploys are unaffected — those take the repo
# contents, not the working directory.
#
# ⚠️  When a .vercelignore exists, Vercel uses it INSTEAD OF .gitignore, so
# everything .gitignore protects has to be repeated here. That is why the
# secrets block below must never be trimmed: .env.local holds the Supabase
# service-role key, and without these lines a CLI deploy would upload it into
# the build context.
#
# Added 2026-07-25, when Vercel stopped producing production builds from git
# pushes (and from a deploy hook) and a direct CLI deploy became the way to ship.
#
# Patterns are root-anchored (`/*.md`, not `*.md`) so they cannot reach into
# src/ or public/. Verified before writing: nothing under src/ imports .md or
# .html, MDX is not configured, and the `@/lib/supabase/*` imports resolve to
# src/lib/ via the tsconfig alias, not the root supabase/ migrations directory.

# ── Secrets — mirrors .gitignore. Never remove. ──────────────────────────────
.env
.env.local
.env*.local
*.pem

# ── Dependencies and build output — mirrors .gitignore ───────────────────────
node_modules/
/.pnp
.pnp.js
/.next/
/out/
/build
/coverage
*.tsbuildinfo
.vercel

# ── Noise — mirrors .gitignore ───────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# ── Not needed to build the app ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# None of these are imported by src/. Excluding them keeps the upload small and
# keeps internal working material out of the deployment.
#
# ⚠️  "Not imported by src/" is NOT the same test as "not needed at runtime".
# docs/legal/mcp-tos.md is never imported: src/lib/mcp-auth.ts reads it with
# fs.readFile at request time, which no import audit can see. Excluding /docs/
# wholesale therefore shipped a /mcp/terms page that served the "Terms are being
# prepared" fallback instead of the terms, silently, from 2026-07-25 until
# 2026-08-12. next.config.mjs traces the file correctly; it was simply never in
# the upload for the trace to find. Before adding anything here, grep for
# readFile/readFileSync on the path, not just for imports.
/docs/*
!/docs/legal/
/docs/legal/*
!/docs/legal/mcp-tos.md
/data/
/reports/
/scripts/
/supabase/
/.claude/

# ── Working files kept loose in the repo root ────────────────────────────────
# Audits, link-check reports, redesign mockups, drafts. Untracked but NOT
# gitignored, so without these lines a CLI deploy would ship them. Root-anchored
# so src/ and public/ are untouched.
/*.md
/*.txt
/*.docx
/*.html
